  "note": "Test 48, durability around the state and report boundary (Astation's review). A transition's next state and its report intents are persisted in one transaction before any POST; the Station adopts the next state only after that commit. host-b's first ack is lost with the Station's crash before the commit: the host resends it, and the same transition gives the same report_id. A restart after the commit and before delivery delivers it; a 503 is retried with the same report_id and body; a POST that reached the Portal whose answer was lost is sent again after a restart, and the Portal answers its recorded 200. host-b's ack resent after that counts nothing. Two replicas load the same committed state and process host-c's ack: byte-identical states and intents (so the Portal would deduplicate); the first commits, the second's compare-and-swap fails and it processes the ack again on the new state, making nothing. Duplicate acks for the original (M3) and the re-signed (M4) native record count nothing twice. revoked{all_applied} is delivered only after both per-host reports. Each report_id reaches the Portal with one body.",
